### Users module — manual requests (REST Client extension for VS Code)
#
# How to use:
# 1. Install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) in VS Code.
# 2. Open this file. Above each request block you'll see a small
#    "Send Request" link — click it to fire that specific request.
# 3. Make sure the API is running (npm run dev) before sending requests.
# 4. baseUrl comes from the active REST Client environment (bottom-right
#    of VS Code) — see .vscode/settings.json for "local" vs "production".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin token setup (needed for GET /users below)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no endpoint to register as ADMIN directly. Instead, run the seed
# script to create/update an admin user from the ADMIN_SEED_* vars in .env:
#   npm run prisma:seed
# Then log in with those credentials via auth/auth.http (POST /auth/login,
# using ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL/ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD from .env) and paste the
# returned accessToken below.
@adminToken = replace-with-admin-token

# Optional: a token from a regular (non-admin) user, used below to check
# the 403 case. Get it the normal way via POST /auth/login.
@userToken = replace-with-user-token

### List all users (admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Error case: list users without the Authorization header
# No token at all — expect 401 Unauthorized.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### Error case: list users with a non-admin user's token
# Valid token, but the user's role isn't ADMIN — expect 403 Forbidden.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
